    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The total sum of squares measures the total variability in the data, while the model sum of squares measures the amount of variation accounted for by the linear model. As noted in our discussions of univariate regression in Chapter 3, the fraction of total variance explained by a linear model is given by the coefficient of determination,",
