    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The sums of squares have different forms under OLS and GLS. Under OLS, the residuals are assumed to be independent with common variance $ \\sigma_{e}^{2} $. In this case, each observation/residual is weighted equally, and the total sum of squares is simply",
