      "content": "The sums of squares under generalized least-squares (GLS) are slightly different, as we have to correct for heteroscedasticity and/or the lack of independence among the residuals. Assume that the residuals have covariance matrix $ \\sigma_{e}^{2}R $. From Equation A3.10, y is replaced by $ \\mathbf{R}^{-1/2}\\mathbf{y} $ and X is replaced by $ \\mathbf{R}^{-1/2}\\mathbf{X} $ in the above OLS expressions for sums of squares. Hence, the total sum of squares for GLS becomes",
